	(text "CONNECTORS (Node60 harness page; REQ-NET-001: exactly four node conductors: T1S pair, battery, ground)\nAll connector parts are PLACEHOLDERS (generic symbols) until the mating sets are selected and frozen together:\n  housings, terminals, seals, wire sizes and keys (harness page, connector freeze condition).\nJ901 battery input: Metri-Pack 480/630 class, or a dual feed with each feed fused; prove the full 60 A path.\nJ902 power return: matched high-current return; no chassis-only return.\n  Fuse: primary fuse at the battery/source end (off-board); per-feed fuses if dual-fed.\nJ903 T1S: separate sealed two-way twisted pair. ESD (D501/D502) sits right behind this connector (DEC-012).\nJ904 outputs: MX150 sealed, 10 A per output, 14 AWG minimum; validate contact and cavity derating at +125 C.\n  Drawn as one 6-way placeholder: the split into housings is part of the TBD-MX150-SETS selection.\nNo KL15, ignition or local wake input (DEC-007).\nUNVERIFIED (release-blocking): every connector mate, pinout and current rating.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
